hand the volume to the hardware when there are no volume keys

The Miyoo Mini has a volume *wheel* -- an analogue pot on the amplifier --
and no volume buttons. Its `soc:gpio_keys` bitmap carries the sixteen keys
this port maps and neither KEY_VOLUMEUP nor KEY_VOLUMEDOWN, decoded off the
device: `1c1682 0 3000400 3014c002` on a Flip against `101682 0 3000400
3014c002` on the Mini, which is those two bits and nothing else.

slot's volume defaults to 60 and is changed with those keys. On a wheel
device that leaves a level at 60% that nothing on the handheld can raise:
quiet, with no way up and no indication why.

So when no input node advertises either key, both outputs go to 100 and
neither is muted, and the wheel does the only job it can do. Read from the
capability bitmaps rather than from a model name, because a bitmap is what is
actually true -- the same reason `0004` reads them as 32-bit words.

A device with volume keys is untouched: the Mini Flip and the Mini Plus keep
their stored level and their HUD.

Applies to upstream 91499a9.

